ontracted coveted 19 and  gave birth at 38 weeks jamal chubb has  been documenting on social media his  wife sierra's battle with kovid back in  july she was pregnant with their third  child when she contracted the virus  sierra did not get the vaccination  because at the time we did not have the  cdc come out and say they recommended it  for pregnant women and it wasn't fda  approved yet the cdc recommended  pregnant women get the vaccine in august  after sierra was already hospitalized i  do wish we had the information we have  now  wish we had that sooner sierra is still  in the hospital on a ventilator but  she's improving and jamal is hopeful  she'll be able to come home soon  maybe miles is also doing well  we shared austin carrington's story with  jamal  he's living every um  significant other's worst nightmare  right now whoa  look i don't want any other  women to  uh  to pass away because of it i couldn't  think of anyone worse to lose for cbs  mornings medea villarreal arlington  texas  it is one thing to miscarry that's tough  enough but to lose your life  your wife  i can't imagine it i know a lot of imams  to be agonized over this at the  beginning because they didn't know  whether the vaccination was right but  now the evidence seems pretty clear and  it's the right thing to do and if that  doesn't get the message through i don't  know what will for some of these women  and these families out there  maria wonderful report
 

